<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116410" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡσεί</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς
			εἰ,</span></b> 
		Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>as if, as though</i>; with
			various moods: </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> c.
			opt., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴσαν, ὡς εἴ τε πυρὶ χθὼν πᾶσα
					νέμοιτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.780
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				11.389
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.314
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡσεί τε</span> c. subj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρίλησ᾽ ὡς εἴ τε πατὴρ ὃν παῖδα
					φιλήσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.481
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς εἰ</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς
				εἴ τε,</span> c. indic., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕπονθ᾽ ὡς εἴ τε μετὰ κτίλον ἕσπετο
					μῆλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.492
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιάλαν ὡς εἴ τις . . δωρήσεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					7.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in
			comparisons, <i>like, just as,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.59
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				7.36
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				290
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				B.
				11.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				653
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				234
			</span></i> (lyr.), etc.: c. part., <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.374
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				194
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς εἴ τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.474
				</span></i>
			; with verb supplied, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.254
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.112
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡσεί περ</span> c.
			part., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				189
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.163
			</span></i> (nisi leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ περὶ
				σεῦ</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; ὡς εἴ πέρ
			τε</span> with a noun, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Cer.</u>
				215
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς εἴτε</span>”
				<i>as it were,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					1.44
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> with
			Numerals, or measures of time and space, <i>about,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡσεὶ τριήκοντα σταδίων μάλιστά κῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.109
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				1.2.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				24.55
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				14.21
			</span></i>, al.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
